course: dictionary
lesson: 4431
title: Handcuff: a noun and a verb
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can be a thing (a noun) or an action (a verb). «A pair of handcuffs» is the noun: two metal rings joined by a chain. We say handcuffs because there are two rings.
explain: «The police handcuffed the thief» uses handcuff as a verb, an action: to put handcuffs on someone. The -ed ending shows it happened in the past.
explain: Read the clues around the word. Police and prisoners tell you the meaning is about locking someone's hands. In everyday talk, a rule can also «handcuff» you, which means it stops you acting freely.
fact: Handcuffs are two metal rings joined by a chain, locked round a prisoner's wrists.
fact: «Handcuff» can be a verb too: «The police handcuffed the thief.»
fact: «Handcuffed» means had handcuffs put on, as in «Toad has been handcuffed».
fact: Informal meaning: a rule or a problem can «handcuff» you, limiting what you can do.
fact: «Ignominiously» means shamefully, so «flung into the water ignominiously» means thrown in a shameful way.
exercise: «The police handcuffed the thief.» What does handcuffed mean here? | *Put handcuffs on the thief | Gave the thief a prize | Chased the thief down the street | Let the thief go free
exercise: «In five minutes the hall is empty except for about a dozen weasels lying on the floor, whom Mole handcuffs.» What does Mole do to the weasels? | Feeds them | Counts them slowly | Chases them out of the hall | *Puts handcuffs on them
exercise: A very strict rule can handcuff you. What does handcuff mean here? | Make you laugh out loud | *Limit what you can do | Hold your hand very tightly | Give you a present
test: «A pair of handcuffs» is which kind of word? | *A noun for a thing | An adjective describing a thing | A full stop | A verb for an action
test: The Rat says Toad was «ignominiously flung into the water». What does ignominiously mean? | Quietly | Happily | *Shamefully | Quickly
exam: In which sentence is handcuff a verb? | A pair of handcuffs lay on the table | Please pass me the handcuffs | Toad was taken away in handcuffs | *The police will handcuff the suspect
